Drill 11 — Cross-Sell Depth and Revenue Resilience
Exact task statement
Test whether customers active across more BUs, LOBs, or Entities show more stable and resilient revenue.
Build order
41.	Use the trailing 12-month window.
42.	Calculate BU, LOB, and Entity footprint counts per customer.
43.	Add active month count, trailing revenue, volatility, and recent growth.
44.	Assign cross_sell_band and resilience_flag.
Validation checks
•	Distinct footprint counts must use the same trailing 12-month window for all customers.
•	active_month_count_12m must be between 1 and 12.
•	Classification rules must be documented before use.
Final output template
customer_code	oracle_customer_name	active_month_count_12m	bu_count_12m	lob_count_12m	entity_count_12m	trailing_12m_revenue	avg_monthly_revenue	volatility_score	last_3m_growth_pct	cross_sell_band	resilience_flag
100234	Customer A	12	3	4	2	48200000	4016667	0.19	8.3%	Deep	Strong
Output column definitions
•	cross_sell_band = segmentation based on BU/LOB/Entity breadth.
•	resilience_flag = final stability classification using breadth, growth, and volatility.
•	avg_monthly_revenue = trailing_12m_revenue / 12.

--===================================================================================================
With customer_data as
(Select
	t.rev_mth_dt,
	t.customer_code,
	t.oracle_customer_name,
	t.bu,
	t.entity,
	sum(t.amount) as customer_revenue,
	p.is_trailing_12m
From platinum.txn_normalized t
Left Join platinum.period_reference p
On t.rev_mth_dt = p.month_start
Where p.is_trailing_12m = 1
Group by 
	t.rev_mth_dt,
	t.customer_code,
	t.oracle_customer_name,
	t.bu,
	t.entity,
	p.is_trailing_12m
Order by
	p.is_trailing_12m desc,
	t.rev_mth_dt
)
Select
	customer_code,
	oracle_customer_name,
	Count(Distinct rev_mth_dt) as active_months,
	Count(distinct bu) as bu_count_12m,
	Count(distinct entity) as entit_count_12m,
	Sum(customer_revenue) as ttm_revenue,
	Round((Sum(customer_revenue) / 12),0) as avg_monthly_rev,
	Round(Stddev_samp(customer_revenue) / Nullif((Sum(customer_revenue) / 12),0),2)  as vol_score
From
	customer_data
Group by 
customer_code,
oracle_customer_name

